{
  "id": "course-enrolment",
  "name": "Course Enrolment",
  "difficulty": "hl",
  "summary": "A higher-level dataset for grouped calculations, joins, averages, views, and HAVING clauses.",
  "focus": [
    "JOIN",
    "GROUP BY",
    "HAVING",
    "AVG"
  ],
  "relationshipHighlights": [
    "One-to-many",
    "Many-to-many",
    "Composite key"
  ],
  "defaultQuery": "SELECT d.DepartmentName, COUNT(*) AS EnrolledCount, ROUND(AVG(e.Score), 1) AS AverageScore FROM ENROLLMENT e JOIN COURSE c ON e.CourseID = c.CourseID JOIN DEPARTMENT d ON c.DepartmentID = d.DepartmentID GROUP BY d.DepartmentName HAVING COUNT(*) >= 4 ORDER BY AverageScore DESC;",
  "notes": [
    "ENROLLMENT is a junction table with a composite key made from StudentID and CourseID.",
    "Grouped queries can summarise how many students each department has and what their average score is."
  ],
